\n<p>Statement 2 : The linear momentum of an isolated system remains constant. The statement is true.</p>"}},"subject":"physics","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":200000,"topic":"torque","type":"mcq","year":2007,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"iit-jee-2007-paper-2-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"1lg4epolf","chapter":"laws-of-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"iit-jee-2007-paper-2-offline","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 2 Offline","permalink":"pstatement-1p-pa-cloth-covers-a-table-some-dishes-ar-jee-advanced-physics-motion-7hbfmeflcc2rhtpp","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>STATEMENT 1</p>\n<p>A cloth covers a table. Some dishes are kept on it. The cloth can be pulled out without dislodging the dishes from the table.</p>\n<p>STATEMENT 2</p>\n<p>For every action there is an equal and opposite reaction.</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement-1 is True, Statement-2 is True; Statement-2 is a correct explanation for Statement-1."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement-1 is True, Statement-2 is True; Statement-2 is NOT a correct explanation for Statement-1s."},{"identifier":"C","content":" Statement-1 is True, Statement-2 is False."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement-1 is False, Statement-2 is True."}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>Statement 1 : Cloth can be pulled out without dislodging the dishes from the table because of inertia. Therefore, statement 1 true.</p>\n<p>Statement 2 : This is Newton's third law and hence true. But statement 2 is not a correct explanation of statement 1 .</p>"}},"subject":"physics","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":200000,"topic":"newtons-laws-of-motion","type":"mcq","year":2007,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"iit-jee-2007-paper-2-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"1lg4es9en","c